    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d128">

                <pb facs="0169" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/7–344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-03T22:00:00-04:00">July 3, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2048. From White<anchor n="28" xml:id="d128-f1"/> for Donnelly.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d128-f2"/>
                </p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>Representatives of the Department and other interested agencies have
                        reached an understanding with Souza Costa<anchor n="30" xml:id="d128-f3"/>
                        under which the National Coffee Department will assure the sale of 1,500,000
                        bags of suitable quality coffee for August shipment to the United States,
                        1,000,000 of which will be for the armed forces. In addition, Brazil has
                        assured the sale of a total of 1,000,000 bags monthly of suitable quality
                        for the months September through December.</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>In order to meet Army requirements and to avoid rationing, it is
                        imperative that this program be executed expeditiously and in full.</item>
                </list>
                <p>Souza Costa has informed National Coffee Department of the above and is awaiting
                    latter’s confirmation that program will be met. Please keep in close touch with
                    Guedes and trade and inform Department by telegram of prospects for execution of
                    understanding. [White.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d128-f1" n="28" xml:id="d128-f1-content">
                <p>Telephoned by Ivan B. White from Bretton Woods, New Hampshire.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d128-f2" n="29" xml:id="d128-f2-content">
                <p>Walter J. Donnelly, Counselor of Embassy for Economic Affairs in Brazil.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d128-f3" n="30" xml:id="d128-f3-content">
                <p>Reference is to the Memorandum of Understanding signed at Bretton Woods, N.H.,
                    July 4; text transmitted to Rio de Janeiro in airgram A–932, July 6, <ref
                        target="#pg632">p. 632</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
